    <string name="teacher_caption">TEACHER NOTES</string>
    <string name="teacher_note_one">Every clue scale is a balanced equation. Two triangles resting against one square is the sentence 2t = s written in brass instead of ink.</string>
    <string name="teacher_note_two">Solving the test scale is substitution. Learners trade a heavy shape for the lighter shapes it balances until only the asked-for shape is left.</string>
    <string name="teacher_note_three">Switch on algebra symbols once the beam feels familiar. The notation then describes something the learner already knows how to do.</string>
